            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TigresMom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's Dungeness crab season, here in San Francisco, and I grew up with Crab Louie. I love this RECIPE! I used cocktail sauce instead of the chlil sauce. Totally delish!",
            "datePublished": "2021-03-05T01:58:49.223Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Definitely five stars for the ingredients in the salad. Colorful and a nice blend of textures and flavors. I used chopped Romaine and Alaskan King Crab, and prepared this as a stacked salad. The dressing is just acceptable; nothing to either love or hate about it. It was a good starting point but needed lift and character - three stars, average. Taking both the salad ingredients and the dressing into consideration, this was a four star salad.",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-04T19:00:45.650Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jo Bowman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The only thing I did outside the recipe was to use Thousand Island dressing instead of making my own. It was really good and we will have it again. This is a good, Summer main course salad.",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-11T23:08:20.807Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DELTAQUEEN50"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a great salad for a warm summer evening. I followed the recipe exactly but added sliced green onions to the salad and a touch of horseradish to the dressing to spice it up a bit. Excellent.",
            "datePublished": "2009-09-26T10:28:21.663Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "COOK471"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Followed the recipe as stated except I used lots of artificial crab as that is what I had instead of real crab meat. When I made a crab Louis salad I usually put a 1000 Island dressing on it but this is so much better. I will always use this dressing. The salad is very refreshing with lots of fresh lemon juice.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-02T18:13:36.420Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BBARTLETT"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this! Was so very tasty, easy to prepare and pretty on the plate. I used bagged lettuce salad for easy, and I prefer cold eggs &amp; cold shrimp on lettuce, so you recommend preparing those items first, to allow for time to chill. Thanks for a GREAT recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2008-02-18T10:14:10.717Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LemonLush"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a nice salad and yes, I made it with the dressing as directed. I also made a Bleu Cheese dressing and served it as a second choice. I'm with the other reviewer, love my hard boiled eggs chilled. Good recipe, thanks for sharing!",
            "datePublished": "2006-09-22T09:38:55.780Z"
          },
          {
